  "final": "`DocumentService.archive` in `src/service.ts` now checks visibility and permission before it changes anything. `tsc -p tsconfig.json && node checks/public.cjs` passes.\n\n- **Visibility:** a missing document, a deleted one, or one in another tenant throws `Error('not found')`. This applies to every role, admin included, and it is checked before permission.\n- **Permission:** an admin may archive any visible document. An editor may archive only a document they own. A viewer never may, and any other role value is also refused. Anyone refused on a visible document gets `Error('forbidden')`.\n- **Success:** it calls the existing `repository.archive`, which sets `archived` to true and appends `{actor: actor.user, document: id}` to the audit.\n- **Repeat archive:** an already archived visible document does nothing, with no new audit entry. The permission check still runs first, so an unauthorized actor gets `forbidden` even then.\n- **Failures:** every throw happens before any write, so documents and audit stay unchanged.\n\nI appended a block to `checks/public.cjs` covering:\n- the three not-found cases for admin and viewer;\n- forbidden for an editor on someone else's document, a viewer, and an editor repeating on an already archived document they don't own;\n- no changes after those failures;\n- successful archives by an editor and an admin;\n- an admin repeat producing no extra audit entry.\n\nI didn't change any public interfaces.",
